  "id": "Kingston-26_00338_FUL",
  "appeal_status": null,
  "appeal_start_date": null,
  "description": "Increase in occupancy from a 7-person (Sui Generis use) HMO to a 9-person Large House in Multiple Occupation (Sui Generis)",
  "development_type": "Minor all other minor developments",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development hereby permitted shall begin before the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.\r\rReason: This is required by Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended).",
    "The refuse and recycling enclosure as shown in the approved details (Drawing: 0326 PL48A) shall be provided prior to beneficial occupation of the two additional HMO bedrooms (No.'s 8 and 9) and shall be permanently retained thereafter. The developer and/or their successors in title shall take all reasonable steps to ensure that all refuse and recyclable materials associated with the development are either stored within these facilities or internally within the building(s) on the application site, and that no refuse or recycling material is stored or placed for collection on the public highway except on the day of collection.\r\rReason: To ensure proper waste management in the interests of the character and appearance of the area and the living conditions of neighbouring occupiers, in accordance with policy SI 7 of the London Plan 2021 and policies CS9 and DM10 of the LDF Core Strategy 2012.",
    "The cycle storage enclosure as shown in the approved details (Drawing: 0326 PL47) shall be provided prior to beneficial occupation of the two additional HMO bedrooms (No.'s 8 and 9) to which this permission relates and shall be permanently retained for that purpose and kept free from obstruction thereafter.\r\rReason: To ensure that appropriate opportunities to promote sustainable transport are taken up, in accordance with policy T5 of the London Plan 2021 and policies CS6 and DM8 of the LDF Core Strategy 2012.",
    "The new shared shower room & W/C (2nd floor) as shown in the approved details (Drawing: 0326 PL45) shall be provided prior to beneficial occupation of the two additional HMO bedrooms (No.'s 8 and 9) to which this permission relates and shall be permanently retained for that purpose and kept free from obstruction thereafter.\r\rReason: To ensure satisfactory living conditions for future residential occupiers, in accordance with policy D3 of the London Plan 2021 and policy DM10 of the LDF Core Strategy 2012.\r\r\r",
    "The facing materials used in the development for the alteration to the front boundary wall to which this permission relates shall match those of the existing building(s) unless otherwise agreed in writing by the local planning authority.\r\rReason: To ensure a satisfactory appearance on completion of the development, in accordance with policy D3 of the London Plan 2021 and policies CS8 and DM10 of the LDF Core Strategy 2012.",
    "The development shall be carried out in accordance with the approved details of the submitted Fire Strategy Statement.\r\rReason: To ensure that the risk of fire is appropriately addressed in the proposed development, in accordance with the Policy D12 of the London Plan (2021).",
    "The mains water consumption of the two additional HMO bedrooms (No.'s 8 and 9) hereby approved shall be compliant with the Optional Requirement set out in Part G of the Building Regulations of 105 litres or less per head per day. \r\rReason: In order to minimise the use of mains water and to comply with Policy SI 5 of the London Plan 2021."
  ],
